        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Memotech MTX500, MTX512, RS128, TEC-1\n- Companies: Memotech, Talking Electronics\n- Systems: Zilog Z80A processor-based home computers, single-board kit computers\n- Places: Australia\n- Topics: home computing, hobbyist electronics\n\nFacts:\n- The TEC-1 was first produced in the early 1980s by the Australian hobbyist electronics magazine Talking Electronics.\n- The TEC-1 is a single-board kit computer.\n- Memotech released the MTX500, MTX512, and RS128 in 1983 and 1984.\n- The Memotech MTX500, MTX512, and RS128 were a series of home computers based on the Zilog Z80A processor.",
